+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+`POST /v1/executions/{id}/signal` answers a recognised idempotent retry (same `Idempotency-Key`, same body, same actor) with the current status and an `idempotency` proof block (`recognizedRetry`, `originalDecisionSequence`), but without the `signalId` the first reply carried. A client that retried after losing the acknowledgement therefore cannot match its request to the recorded signal — the very identification the retry mechanism exists to restore. The id is already durable in the store (the committed `signal_recorded` event's payload); it is simply not read back.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A recognised retry of `execution.signal` over the Public Runtime API now carries the original durable `signalId` in the reply `data`, sourced from the committed `signal_recorded` decision event that authenticated the retry — not recomputed from the request body.
+- A mismatched actor or a wrong-kind event under the same key still gets no retry proof and no `signalId` (the refusal shapes are unchanged).
+- Regression assertions added to the existing HTTP tests in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`: the recognised-signal-retry test asserts the reply carries the original `signalId`, and the mismatched-actor / wrong-kind tests assert no `signalId` appears. The positive assertion fails against the current code.
+
+Assumption (recorded per unattended-run rules): the field is added at top-level `data.signalId`, mirroring the fresh-success shape, rather than inside the `idempotency` block, whose exact shape is equality-asserted by existing tests and must keep passing unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `mutation-idempotency`: idempotent-retry classification and reply contract for execution mutations served over the Public Runtime API — which replies count as recognised retries, what proof those replies carry (including durable command-specific identifiers such as the signal id), and which replies must carry no proof at all.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+(none — `openspec/specs/` holds no existing capabilities)
+
+## Impact
+
+- `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` — idempotency key classification (`classify_one_key` / `classify_existing_keys`) carries the matched event's durable signal id through `KeyState::Complete` into the recognised-retry reply path (`reply_with_current_status` → `annotate_recognized_retry`).
+- `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs` — regression assertions on the existing retry tests.
+- Additive-only wire change on the recognised-retry success shape of one endpoint. No core-crate, schema, event-store, or CLI-envelope changes; no new dependencies.
