+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Regression assertions (RED)
+
+Reference: `openspec/specs/mutation-idempotency/spec.md` requirements "Recognised signal retry returns the original durable signal identifier" and "Refused retries carry no retry proof and no signal identifier". All edits are in `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`, extending existing tests only.
+
+- [x] 1.1 In `a_retried_mutation_with_the_same_idempotency_key_appends_nothing`, after the existing `idempotency`-block assertion, assert `retry_reply["data"]["signalId"]` equals `original_event["kind"]["data"]["signalId"]` (the committed payload's id, `"signal-http-retry"`), proving the value is read from the store. Verify: `cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --test api_http -- a_retried_mutation_with_the_same_idempotency_key_appends_nothing -- --exact` FAILS on the current tree (missing `signalId`), confirming the assertion observes the gap.
+- [x] 1.2 In `the_same_key_and_body_from_a_different_actor_is_not_a_recognized_retry` and `an_event_of_the_wrong_kind_with_the_same_key_is_not_a_recognized_retry`, assert the refused reply's `data` carries no `signalId` (`get("signalId").is_none()`), beside the existing no-`idempotency` assertions. Verify: run both tests by name the same way as 1.1; both PASS on the current tree (they guard the negative side of the contract).
+
+## 2. Serve layer: carry the durable signal id into the retry reply
+
+Reference: `design.md` decisions 1–4. Single file: `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs`.
+
+- [x] 2.1 Extend the classification to carry the id: widen `KeyPresence::Present` and `KeyState::Complete` to hold the matched event's signal id (`Option<String>`); extract it in `classify_one_key` only on the exact-key + full-match path and only when `expected.kind` is `MutationDecisionKind::SignalRecorded` (clone from the payload the match already verified); keep `Divergent`/`Partial` untouched and update the enum doc comments accordingly. Verify: `cargo +1.97.1 clippy -p graphhelm-cli --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` is clean, the 1.1 test still fails (behavior not yet wired), and no other `KeyState`/`KeyPresence` call site was missed (grep).
+- [x] 2.2 Wire the id into the reply: thread the option through both `KeyState::Complete` call sites in `run_idempotent_mutation_inner` into `reply_with_current_status` → `reply_with_status_value` → `annotate_recognized_retry`, which inserts top-level `data.signalId` only when the option is present; refresh the reply-shape doc comments on those functions. Verify: the 1.1 test now PASSES (RED→GREEN), both 1.2 tests stay green, and non-signal command replies are unchanged (their option stays `None`).
+
+## 3. Integration checks
+
+- [x] 3.1 Confirm the shared recognised-retry path is undisturbed for non-signal mutations: run `an_equivalent_fractional_sweep_instant_is_still_an_exact_retry` and `a_null_wake_cursor_retries_the_server_derived_arming` by name in the same test binary; both must PASS.
+- [x] 3.2 Run the serve module's own unit tests (`cargo +1.97.1 test -p graphhelm-cli --lib -- serve -- --nocapture` or the equivalent filter for `commands::serve`) and `cargo +1.97.1 fmt --all -- --check`; both must be clean.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- The PR body carries the Keel three-line card: in-scope paths (`apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs`, `apps/cli/tests/api_http.rs`), the promise (recognised `execution.signal` retry returns the original durable `signalId`; mismatched actor and wrong-kind still get no proof and no `signalId`), and the proof command from 1.1 plus the green runs from 1.2, 3.1, 3.2.
+- Review per `docs/process/DELIVERY.md`: one review by a session or blind subagent that did not write the change, running the named tests; delivery requires merge into `main`.
